window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-fe99c01976e8150f"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"scan-code-changes-for-security\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">扫描代码变更中的安全问题</h1> <p>检查拉取请求或本地差异是否引入安全回归。</p> <p>使用 Codex Security 插件检查基于 Git 的变更集，验证可信的安全回归迹象，并在合并前生成有证据支持的报告。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>涉及身份验证、授权、解析、文件访问、机密信息或特权工作流的拉取请求。</li> <li>合并前需要进行安全专项检查的发布分支或本地补丁。</li> <li>需要将发现对应到变更代码和直接支持文件的审查人员。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">$codex-security:security-diff-scan</a></td> <td>检查拉取请求、提交、分支差异或工作树补丁中的安全回归，并通过验证和攻击路径证据支撑结论。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>检查变更是否引入安全回归</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $codex-security:security-diff-scan 检查此 PR、提交、分支差异或工作树补丁是否引入安全回归。\n\n范围和规则：\n- 目标：[this pull request / commit SHA / branch diff from BASE to HEAD / the current working-tree patch]\n- 我已获得评估此代码库和变更集的授权。\n- 请重点关注 [auth, input handling, secrets, filesystem, network, dependencies, or other sensitive surface]。\n\n请返回最终 Markdown 报告，并对需要人工审查的发现添加行内代码评论。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">安全变更审查指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/github-code-reviews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">审查 GitHub 拉取请求（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent 审批与安全</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"review-the-change-instead-of-the-whole-repository\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">检查变更，而不是整个代码库</h2> <p>当拉取请求、提交、分支或本地补丁改动了敏感代码路径时，可以使用安全差异扫描。Codex Security 插件会结合代码库上下文理解变更，并将问题发现和验证范围聚焦在差异及其直接相关代码上。</p> <p>这种工作流可补充常规代码审查。如果你需要的是关于安全回归的证据，而不是一般性的代码风格或测试审查，就适合使用它。</p> <p><a id=\"run-a-focused-pass\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">执行定向检查</h2> <ol> <li>打开代码库，并检出或说明要审查的确切 Git 变更集。</li> <li>完成 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security 插件快速入门（本地尚未收录）</a>，并在起步提示词中指定拉取请求、提交、分支差异或工作树补丁。</li> <li>列出变更中需要重点关注的高风险部分，例如身份验证、解析器、文件路径、网络请求或凭据处理。</li> <li>运行提示词时先不要要求修复，以便第一份结果保留为审查记录。</li> <li>在决定是否修复前，逐项检查报告所指的受影响代码行、验证结果和明确指出的证据缺口。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"follow-through-on-a-finding\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">跟进安全发现</h2> <p>有用的报告会区分可触达且有证据支持的安全问题，与仍需确认的怀疑；还可以对受影响代码添加行内评论。对于可采取行动的发现，请创建范围明确的新修复任务，并附上发现编号或报告中的相关部分。关于修复和验证流程，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复漏洞待办列表（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p>关于变更选择器、差异范围和结果审查，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin/code-changes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">审查代码变更以查找安全问题（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"scan-code-changes-for-security\">Scan code changes for security</h1> <p>Review a pull request or local diff for security regressions.</p> <p>Use the Codex Security plugin to examine a Git-backed change set, validate plausible security regressions, and produce an evidence-based report before merge.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Pull requests that touch authentication, authorization, parsing, file access, secrets, or privileged workflows.</li> <li>Release branches or local patches that need a security-focused check before merge.</li> <li>Reviewers who need findings anchored to changed code and directly supporting files.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">$codex-security:security-diff-scan</a></td> <td>Review a pull request, commit, branch diff, or working-tree patch for security regressions with validation and attack-path evidence.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Review a Change for Security Regressions</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:security-diff-scan to review this PR, commit, branch diff, or working-tree patch for security regressions.\n\nScope and rules:\n- Target: [this pull request / commit SHA / branch diff from BASE to HEAD / the current working-tree patch]\n- I am authorized to assess this repository and change set.\n- Pay particular attention to [auth, input handling, secrets, filesystem, network, dependencies, or other sensitive surface].\n\nReturn the final Markdown report and inline code comments for findings that require human review.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">Security change-review guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/github-code-reviews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Review GitHub pull requests (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent approvals and security</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"review-the-change-instead-of-the-whole-repository\">Review the change instead of the whole repository</h2> <p>Use a security diff scan when a pull request, commit, branch, or local patch changes a sensitive code path. The Codex Security plugin uses repository context to understand the change, then keeps finding discovery and validation focused on the diff and directly supporting code.</p> <p>This workflow complements ordinary code review. Use it when you want evidence about security regressions, not a general style or test review.</p> <h2 id=\"run-a-focused-pass\">Run a focused pass</h2> <ol> <li>Open the repository and check out or describe the exact Git-backed change set to review.</li> <li>Complete the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security plugin quickstart (not in this local snapshot)</a> and specify the pull request, commit, branch diff, or working-tree patch in the starter prompt.</li> <li>Name high-risk surfaces in the change, such as authentication, parsers, file paths, network requests, or credential handling.</li> <li>Run the prompt without requesting a fix so the first result remains a review artifact.</li> <li>Check each reported affected line, validation result, and stated proof gap before deciding whether to remediate.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"follow-through-on-a-finding\">Follow through on a finding</h2> <p>A useful report distinguishes a reachable, supported security finding from a suspicion that still needs confirmation and can include inline code comments for affected lines. For an actionable result, open a new bounded fix task with the finding identifier or the relevant report section. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Remediate a vulnerability backlog (not in this local snapshot)</a> for the fix-and-validation loop.</p> <p>For change selectors, diff scope, and result review, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin/code-changes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Review code changes for security (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p>"};
